{
  "dom_id": "step-t1823",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "A **piecewise function** is a function that is defined differently in different parts of the function's domain.\n\nFor example, consider the piecewise function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/a8e8a9c3f9a7bef1c9c40cad27eeb93267b8b30eb74ce36acd9bf90b461c21ae.svg) defined as follows:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/78daf51ed18581f874f275e211d9f6b651af383503fdbc6e04f7d06b083eaffd.svg)\nA plot of the function is given below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/2ad96db45424ed30eb3219a4ae36e13d5498a3719695ccb73a9313058f2fa15c.png)\n\nThe function has two distinct branches, one for  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/a3d6121723fd4e9feea862013f28e4326de8afabb08b46040ca1c80788500f84.svg) and one for  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/ee98d74fc058e95e72d13a5e575e70e4d5adedd26413e3f01ab1e3f788be87e8.svg). The function is a piecewise function because it has different definitions depending on where we are in the domain. \n\nSuppose that we want to calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/0c0dc4f7a3b289c14dd126e050458eab6b82ccccb923d9c6993ac5042303568e.svg) For this, we'd use the  left branch ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/a3d6121723fd4e9feea862013f28e4326de8afabb08b46040ca1c80788500f84.svg) because ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/8521c0711d7afa3552209b26e08d80787124feea347c2cdfa81a8de5470ab58d.svg) On this branch, the function definition is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/5d344346082f57f1cd7456779e9a30d079068f78a466fe899ac376cfbd14dbaf.svg) so we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/0e990ed7688ceb39db8d63fd54c0f22f52f5260efb6636419319b92b43171610.svg)\n\nSimilarly, if we want to calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/713ad3a0e19cfab825d702bd00e14c956db1844974c9da945d697930a02e7178.svg), we'd use the  right branch ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/ee98d74fc058e95e72d13a5e575e70e4d5adedd26413e3f01ab1e3f788be87e8.svg) because ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/95a3686bf6cd3fddc29b98a39ab23027d1cc794ae2517aefde675a62f0a4d023.svg) On this branch, the function definition is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/85f568b3e2d870a755a97fb3457f3c62e814f559b8b017ac05c291fb5d8aa79e.svg) so we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/166c6a001bb66b83e3d369c2211f11baf60650e54c93da7bee47539fa717d44a.svg)",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
